    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code and won't start. what am i supposed to do to fix this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The E15 error on a Bosch dishwasher typically indicates a fault with the circulation pump, often meaning the motor is jammed or burnt out. Before attempting complex repairs, try unplugging the unit for five minutes to reset the electronic control, then check if the drain hose is properly connected without kinks that could block water flow. If the issue persists after this reset, replacing the circulation pump motor is usually required, but since this involves high voltage and disassembly, you should contact Bosch customer service or a professional appliance repair technician. Do not force the dishwasher to run, as this will likely damage the motor further.",
