      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Wiping up water from the bottom of the base pan is usually insufficient to clear an E15 error, as the sensor often detects moisture within the pump's motor housing itself. You would need to remove the drip pan and carefully disassemble the pump, but forcing a jammed motor dry often fails because internal bearings may be seized rather than just wet. Given that modern Bosch pumps are precise electronic units, professional diagnosis is highly recommended before attempting any further DIY disassembly.",
