      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Trying to dry out moisture with a hairdryer is dangerous and likely ineffective, as it only dries the exterior of the drip pan and will not remove the root cause if the pump sensors are internally saturated. You can typically remove the bottom door panel of the dishwasher to access the base pan without moving the entire machine, use a cup to pump out the water, and carefully weigh it down to check for heavy debris. However, if the circulation pump itself is the issue, once you dry the base panel, the error will almost certainly return.",
